# Workflow Invariants

- Treat generation, review, scheduling, posting, and analytics as distinct states.
- Never bypass approval-first flow by auto-posting unless the user explicitly asks for an override.
- Persist generated platform payloads before any delayed or scheduled posting path uses them.
- Keep review state explicit and durable; do not rely on transient in-memory values.
- When changing workflow behavior, update the storage layer, CLI surface, and tests together.

Example:

- Bad: regenerate captions during posting because they were never stored.
- Good: write captions and hashtags to persistent payload records before review or scheduling.
